WEBVTT

00:01.600 --> 00:05.100
Every app ends up with a table.

00:05.200 --> 00:10.340
It's where the real work happens. So it should be the best part.

00:11.200 --> 00:15.220
Meet Tally, an open-source data table.

00:15.400 --> 00:21.580
Every column knows its type. So money looks like money, and people look like people.

00:22.900 --> 00:30.600
Write a filter. Each condition finds its column, and everything else falls away.

00:32.000 --> 00:39.900
Or just ask in plain English. You get a real filter back, one you can read and keep.

00:40.000 --> 00:48.100
Point Tally at a live source, and every change streams straight in. Values update in place, and rows re-rank on their own.

00:48.200 --> 00:55.100
Copy, paste, fill down. Change your mind, and every step undoes cleanly.

00:56.600 --> 01:01.820
Group by anything, with the totals already worked out.

01:04.000 --> 01:08.420
Need an answer that isn't in your data? Add an AI column, and it works through every row.

01:11.200 --> 01:17.140
Under every view is one clean request. Tally checks it, then speaks your database's language.

01:20.800 --> 01:29.700
React, Vue, Svelte or Solid. Postgres, Laravel, Supabase, or your own API. Bring the stack you already have.

01:29.800 --> 01:36.460
Make the screen smaller, and Tally adapts. Columns step aside, rows become cards, and details are one tap away.

01:38.600 --> 01:45.820
And when you want it your way, just ask your coding agent. It knows exactly where each change goes.

01:47.500 --> 01:51.600
Customize every piece, so it fits your design system and your stack.

01:51.700 --> 01:57.240
Tally. Open source, and ready for your next big idea.
